<%# The status pill on a Ranked row, split out so a status change can be
    broadcast into an open queue without re-rendering the row around it.

    Deliberately NOT the shared `_status_badge` partial: that one carries the
    `session_<id>_status_badge` DOM id the detail page's live region owns, and a
    session listed on the Ranked view while its detail drawer is open would then
    have two elements claiming the same id. It is also sized for a card.

    A running session spins. The queue is read to answer "what is actually moving
    right now", and a colour alone does not carry that across a column of forty
    rows. Same spinner the card grid's badge uses, sized down for a row, and it
    arrives and leaves with the pill because the pill is what the ranked stream
    replaces.

    `motion-safe:` rather than a bare `animate-spin`: a reader who asked their OS
    for reduced motion gets the glyph without the rotation. The pill's own
    "Running" text is the accessible name either way, which is why the svg is
    `aria-hidden` — labelling it would have a screen reader announce "Running
    running".

    Locals:
      agent_session - the session %>
<span id="ranked_row_status_<%= agent_session.id %>" data-live-region="replace"
      class="inline-flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1 rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium <%= status_badge_classes(agent_session) %>">
  <% if agent_session.status == "running" %>
    <svg class="h-3 w-3 shrink-0 motion-safe:animate-spin" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
      <circle class="opacity-25" cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="4"></circle>
      <path class="opacity-75" fill="currentColor" d="M4 12a8 8 0 018-8V0C5.373 0 0 5.373 0 12h4zm2 5.291A7.962 7.962 0 014 12H0c0 3.042 1.135 5.824 3 7.938l3-2.647z"></path>
    </svg>
  <% end %>
  <span><%= agent_session.archived? ? "Trashed" : agent_session.status.humanize %></span>
</span>
